Fillets: a rounding whose contact runs off its face across an edge that
leads into the end vertex tangent to the rounding's other face rolls on
that edge up to the vertex, where it vanishes (mitcad#343).

The case: a post of radius 10 under a block as wide as the post (the
post's top circle touches the block's long bottom edges at two points,
where the block's underside narrows to nothing and the post's side is
tangent to the block's long sides). The post's foot rounded with 10: the
underside's contact (20 from the axis) runs off the underside across its
long edges 30 degrees from the long axis; from there the ball rolls on
those edges, touching the post, up to the points where they touch the
post's top circle: the edges run into those points tangent to the post's
side, the ball has no room left and the rounding vanishes there (as in
the bodies stored in the file). OCCT took those edges, which end at the
rounding's end vertex, for no obstacle there (StartSol: an arc at the
end vertex is the face at the end's), ended each side's rounding where
the contact left the underside and extended it with tangent planes; the
corners at the two points filled the rest wrongly, an invalid result.

- StartSol: an arc that holds the end vertex is still an obstacle, the
  ball rolling on it, where it runs into the vertex tangent to the
  blend's other face (ChFi3d_ArcTangentToFaceAt: its direction there in
  that face's tangent plane within 0.01 rad). No face at the end can cut
  such a blend at the vertex.
- PerformFilletOnVertex: several roundings ending at one vertex, each
  vanishing there (its contacts within a hundredth of its radius of the
  vertex, its faces' normals there parallel within 0.002 rad, or already
  ending in a point at it), each end in a point at the vertex
  (ChFi3d_ShrinkVanishingEnd, so far for a rounding ending alone there),
  and the corner is the singular one. ChFi3d_ShrinkVanishingEnd: the
  faces' normals are taken at the contacts' ends (a face's surface may
  degenerate at the vertex itself), an end whose contacts coincide short
  of the vertex is moved too, a check without moving (theApply), the end
  parameters matched within a thousand times the parametric confusion
  (they are carried through sums), and before the end poles are moved
  the contact curves are cut by full knots where they are twice the
  end's distance from the vertex, so that only that last piece bends.

Upstream: new.
